{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1283616","title":"Research on the Impact of temperature on the performance of the SADA system and the Interactions among Microorganisms","description":"Sulfur-driven autotrophic denitrification coupled with anaerobic ammonium oxidation (SADA) has gained significant attention due to its high-efficiency potential for synchronous nitrogen removal. However, the regulatory mechanisms of temperature variation on the performance of the coupled system, sludge properties, and microbial communities remain unclear. This study systematically investigated the effects of low-temperature stress on nitrogen removal efficiency and sludge activity in the SADA system. This was achieved by constructing individual sulfur-driven autotrophic denitrification (SAD) and anammox reactors, coupling these systems, and implementing a stepwise cooling strategy. Furthermore, the dynamics of microbial community diversity and composition in the SADA system in response to temperature changes were revealed using 16S rRNA gene sequencing. Based on random matrix theory (RMT), molecular ecological network analysis was employed to construct microbial co-occurrence networks across the cooling gradient. This approach elucidated the influence of temperature on the assembly mechanisms of the microbial community.","center":"Beijing University of Chemical Technology","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2025/06/29 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN49700845","Metagenome or environmental sample from sludge metagenome","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2025-01-30",2025,"CN","Beijing",1816670,"Beijing","verified",39.8877,116.4343,"China:Beijing","UASB anammox reactor",null,null,null,"city-level location without sampl